tasks.detail:
Goal: Provide a controlled-but-not-re-rendering CodeMirror 6 editor component with the exact prop contract the viewer integration will consume.
Files: create `components/FileEditor.tsx` and `components/FileEditor.test.mjs`. Do not touch `components/FileViewer.tsx` (TASK-008) or any i18n file (TASK-004).
Contract: props are exactly
  export interface FileEditorProps {
    value: string;
    language: string;
    wrapLines: boolean;
    readOnly?: boolean;
    onChange: (next: string) => void;
    onSave?: () => void;
    onReady?: () => void;
  }
Behaviour requirements:
- `"use client"` at the top. Create exactly one `EditorView` in a `useEffect` with `[]` deps, mounted into a `div` ref, and `view.destroy()` in cleanup. The component must hold **no** React state for the text: `onChange` fires from an `EditorView.updateListener` when `update.docChanged`, and the current `value`/`language`/`wrapLines`/`onChange`/`onSave` are read through refs updated on every render.
- Extensions: `lineNumbers()`, `highlightActiveLine()`, `history()`, `keymap.of([...defaultKeymap, ...historyKeymap, indentWithTab, { key: "Mod-s", preventDefault: true, run: () => { onSaveRef.current?.(); return true; } }])`, `searchKeymap`, `bracketMatching()`, `EditorView.lineWrapping` only when `wrapLines`, `EditorState.readOnly.of(readOnly ?? false)`, `EditorView.updateListener.of(...)`, and a theme built with `EditorView.theme(...)` from the existing CSS variables (`--bg`, `--text`, `--font-mono`, `--bg-selected`, ...) so light and dark both work without `@codemirror/theme-one-dark`. Use `useTheme()` (`hooks/useTheme.ts`) only to pick the two variant colours.
- When the `value` prop changes from outside and differs from `view.state.doc.toString()`, dispatch a transaction replacing the whole document, preserving selection where possible. When it is equal, dispatch nothing (this is what makes the save echo harmless).
- Language: call `loadLanguageExtension(language)` from `lib/code-languages.ts` (TASK-003) and reconfigure through `Compartment`s when it resolves to a non-null `Extension`; a `null` result leaves the document unhighlighted. The `setLanguage`/`setWrap` reconfiguration must not recreate the `EditorView`.
- `onReady?.()` once after the view is created. Import order/style follows the existing components (`@/` aliases, no default React import unless needed).
Steps:
1. Write `components/FileEditor.tsx` per the contract.
2. Write `components/FileEditor.test.mjs` in the source-assertion style of `components/FileViewer.test.mjs` (read the file, assert with regexes): exactly one `new EditorView(`, exactly one `view.destroy()`, `key: "Mod-s"`, `update.docChanged`, no `useState(` in the component, `EditorView.lineWrapping` guarded by `wrapLines`, and `loadLanguageExtension` imported from `@/lib/code-languages`.
Verify: `node --experimental-strip-types --test components/FileEditor.test.mjs` passes and `node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit` is clean.
Done when: the component compiles, does not re-render per keystroke, exposes the exact props above, and the assertions pass.
